.TH PISTATS-BACKEND 1 "August 2026" "PiStats Backend 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pistats-backend \- run the PiStats Raspberry Pi backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pistats-backend
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pistats-backend
starts the private HTTP API used by PiStats clients. The Debian system service
loads configuration from
.IR /etc/pistats/pistats.env .
.PP
The default configuration listens only on 127.0.0.1:8787 and requires the
generated bearer token. Network exposure, Wake-on-LAN, backup-drive hints, and
media storage are opt-in. Docker monitoring selections are managed by clients.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pistats/pistats.env
Persistent service configuration and bearer token.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pistats
Private service state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ZenDeveloper7/PiStats-Backend
